From 525e1dfc57193ad3edcc493123ed26b3ed598b0d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: kernel86-64 <87580651+kernel86-64@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 22 Nov 2026 19:42:59 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 36/57] ASoC: qdsp6: q6core: never ask the MSM8998 ADSP for its
 versions

The MSM8998 ADSP firmware stops reading its glink FIFO for good when it
receives AVCS_CMD_GET_FWK_VERSION: no crash, no watchdog, just a dead
transport.  Every later APPS->ADSP message then fails with "intent
request timed out", which also kills the SLIMbus QMI service and leaves
the AP without a sound card.  The modem shares the same glink firmware
and eventually dies with "RCECB client callback runtime exceeded".

Mark the versions as already requested on qcom,msm8998 so AFE, ASM and
ADM keep using the legacy APIs this firmware implements.  This is the
same guard the 6.18 tree carries.
---
 sound/soc/qcom/qdsp6/q6core.c | 11 +++++++++++
 1 file changed, 11 insertions(+)

diff --git a/sound/soc/qcom/qdsp6/q6core.c b/sound/soc/qcom/qdsp6/q6core.c
index 48825756a..4016e292f 100644
--- a/sound/soc/qcom/qdsp6/q6core.c
+++ b/sound/soc/qcom/qdsp6/q6core.c
@@ -253,6 +253,17 @@ int q6core_get_svc_api_info(int svc_id, struct q6core_svc_api_info *ainfo)
 		return 0;
 
 	mutex_lock(&g_core->lock);
+	/*
+	 * The MSM8998 ADSP firmware stops reading its glink FIFO for good
+	 * when it receives AVCS_CMD_GET_FWK_VERSION: no crash, no watchdog,
+	 * just a dead transport that also takes the SLIMbus QMI service with
+	 * it. Leave the versions unknown there; AFE, ASM and ADM then use
+	 * their legacy APIs, which this firmware speaks.
+	 */
+	if (!g_core->is_version_requested &&
+	    of_machine_is_compatible("qcom,msm8998"))
+		g_core->is_version_requested = true;
+
 	if (!g_core->is_version_requested) {
 		if (q6core_get_fwk_versions(g_core) == -ENOTSUPP)
 			q6core_get_svc_versions(g_core);
